# CIDOC-CRM / CRMinf alignment

Chrystallum uses CIDOC as an **interop alignment layer**, not native storage.

## Sources (consult before proposing)

1. `CIDOC/cidoc_wikidata_mapping_validated.csv` — Wikidata QID/PID → CRM class/property
2. `Relationships/relationship_types_registry_master.csv` — `cidoc_crm_code`, `crminf_applicable`
3. Neo4j `SYS_RelationshipType.cidoc_crm_code` (synced from CSV)

## Entity typing defaults

| Chrystallum | CIDOC |
|-------------|-------|
| Person | E21_Person |
| Event | E5_Event |
| Place | E53_Place |
| Claim | I2_Belief / E13_Attribute_Assignment |
| CorpusWork | E31_Document / I10_Provenance_Statement |
| SubjectConcept | E28_Conceptual_Object / E55_Type |

## CRMinf claim chain

```
CorpusWork (evidence) → Inference (Fischer / agent) → Claim (I2_Belief) → canonical edge (adopted belief)
```

- Confidence lives on **Claim**, not promoted edges
- Human validation ≈ I7_Belief_Adoption

## Rules

- Prefer relationship types that have `cidoc_crm_code` in the registry
- Do not invent CRM properties when a registry type already maps the Wikidata PID
- If no CIDOC mapping exists, note the gap — do not force a wrong class

Prompt injection: `scripts/tools/cidoc_context.py` via `append_republic_graph_context()`.
